The value of \(\frac{\pi}{3}\) is approximately 1.0472. Since this value is less than 4, according to the piecewise function definition:

\[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
\lfloor n \rfloor & \text{ if }n \geq 4, \\
\lceil n \rceil & \text{ if } n < 4.
\end{array}
\right.\]

we use the second part of the definition, which means \(f\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right) = \lceil \frac{\pi}{3} \rceil\). The ceiling function \(\lceil x \rceil\) returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to \(x\). Therefore, \(\lceil \frac{\pi}{3} \rceil = 2\).

This fits into the piecewise function definition because \(\frac{\pi}{3}\) is less than 4, and thus we apply the ceiling function to round up to the nearest integer.
